# Videos are stored as ordinary git objects, NOT Git LFS.
#
# Vercel does not fetch LFS objects during a build, so LFS-tracked videos
# deployed as pointer stubs and had to be served from GitHub's LFS media
# endpoint at runtime -- which burns the 1 GB/month LFS bandwidth quota.
# As plain files they ship inside the Vercel build output and are served
# from Vercel's CDN instead. Keep them compressed (720p) so the repo and
# the deployment stay small.
*.mp4 -text
*.MP4 -text
*.MOV -text
*.mov -text
